committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1792133799 +0900

G-a: held-out definitions (grammar, seeded draws, gold-only rejection, kappa_set)

gen/kappa.py: a grammar of definitions (source, predicate over records,
aggregate, window, threshold) whose (source, predicate) pairs are disjoint
from the fixed six; v2 changes the threshold or the window. heldout_draw(seed)
samples six definitions with distinct predicates and rejects, from gold on
worlds 1000-1009 only, a candidate whose gold is constant across the post-fork
checkpoints in more than half the worlds or empty/abstain in more than half the
item-checkpoints (either version). evaluate/scope_members resolve held-out ids
(h<seed>_<name>) through one generic evaluator, so gold and the D=1
checker/fallback share it. CLI: python -m memshift.gen.kappa --list-heldout.

gen/world.py: world param kappa_set "heldout:<seed>" swaps the six definition
slots in to_world; the builder keeps the fixed slots, so events and every other
slot are those of the fixed-set world. Fixed-set worlds are byte-identical
(pinned hashes for world 1000, four branches).

